{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>The princes dug it.</b> Moses and Aaron, as it is written: ודברתם אל הסלע." "<b>With the lawgiver, with their staffs.</b> When he struck the rock with the staff, it made an impression in the rock and it split. Like a mark scratched on a wall." "<b>And from the wilderness, Mattanah.</b> This refers back to what is written above: ויחנו בעבר ארנון אשר במדבר etc. — and from that side that is in the wilderness, which is Almon Diblathaim, they came to Mattanah, which is called Har ha'Avarim in the section of the journeys; as it is written there: ויסעו מעלמון דבלתימה ויחנו בהרי העברים לפני נבו. That place is on the northern side of the Arnon valley, at the beginning of the land of Sihon, and it is called Mattanah because there Israel's gift of the land began. And the reason it does not write here 'they journeyed and encamped' is that they were still stationed at the side of the Arnon that is in the wilderness, as it is written in the section of Devarim: ואשלח מלאכים ממדבר קדמות אל סיחון — meaning, from the wilderness that is in the east, not from the wilderness that is in the south. And in that passage the conquest of the land of Sihon is described; and further, since it began to write the journeys, once it starts it goes and finishes, mentioning all of them down to the last one."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:06.421615779Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}